# AIDR — Null / empty display text

When rendering optional or nullable data on **FE UI** (detail cards, tables, summaries):

## Rule

1. **Do not** leave the UI blank, or only show a bare dash `—` / `N/A` with no meaning.
2. Show a **short English phrase** that explains the missing value for that field.
3. Prefer muted styling (`text-muted`) for empty-state copy so it does not look like real data.
4. Reuse helpers in `utils/displayValue.ts` (`displayText`, `displayOptionalNumber`, `isBlank`) and `formatDateTime(value, emptyLabel)`.

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌
<p>{product.brand || '—'}</p>
<p>{formatDateTime(product.publishedAt)}</p> // defaults to "—"

// ✅
<p className={isBlank(product.brand) ? 'text-muted' : undefined}>
  {displayText(product.brand, 'No brand provided')}
</p>
<p className={!product.publishedAt ? 'text-muted' : undefined}>
  {formatDateTime(product.publishedAt, 'Not published yet')}
</p>
```

| Field kind | Suggested empty copy |
|------------|----------------------|
| Brand / model / origin | `No brand provided` / `No model number` / `Origin not specified` |
| Description | `No description provided` |
| Date not set yet | `Not published yet`, `Not reviewed yet` |
| Images / list | `No images uploaded`, `No items yet` |
| Warranty / count | `No warranty listed` |

## Do not

- Invent fake data (fake dates, “0 months”) when the value is truly unknown.
- Mix Vietnamese empty labels on English UI screens.
- Use only `—` on Admin/Seller detail pages where context matters (moderation, returns, inventory).
